1
00:00:27,361 --> 00:00:30,964
(Francesca Next Door)

2
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,635
(All names of people, places, events,
and other details are fictitious.)

3
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,969
(AI-based technology was used
in part of the production.)

4
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:38,472
Take a look at this.

5
00:00:38,939 --> 00:00:42,009
So is this the footage from that accident?

6
00:00:42,075 --> 00:00:45,045
That's right.
It was caught on the dashcam.

7
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:51,018
But...

8
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:54,221
did you bring the thing you promised?

9
00:01:29,022 --> 00:01:30,090
Hey.

10
00:01:30,991 --> 00:01:31,992
You...

11
00:01:36,897 --> 00:01:37,898
What's wrong?

12
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:42,936
It's too overwhelming...

13
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:44,204
What?

14
00:01:46,406 --> 00:01:48,542
Na Young, wake up.

15
00:01:49,309 --> 00:01:50,410
What's wrong with you?

16
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:55,816
Hey, can you hear me?

17
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:03,991
Did she have any symptoms
before she fell unconscious?

18
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:06,226
I'm not sure.

19
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:09,296
She passed out
after having trouble breathing.

20
00:02:09,363 --> 00:02:11,231
Check her blood pressure
and oxygen saturation,

21
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:13,000
and hook her up to an ECG.

22
00:02:13,066 --> 00:02:14,067
Okay.

23
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,502
Is it really bad?

24
00:02:16,069 --> 00:02:17,904
She looks fine on the outside.

25
00:02:18,739 --> 00:02:22,209
Do you know her medical history
or what medications she's taking?

26
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,845
I don't really know.

27
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,580
Does she have a guardian?

28
00:02:26,913 --> 00:02:27,914
A guardian...

29
00:02:29,383 --> 00:02:30,417
So that's...

30
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:34,755
Oh, hold on.

31
00:02:39,393 --> 00:02:40,460
(September 12, Saturday)

32
00:02:40,527 --> 00:02:42,629
She'd have his number.

33
00:02:43,664 --> 00:02:45,065
(Butler Francisco)

34
00:02:45,732 --> 00:02:46,833
"Butler."

35
00:02:47,701 --> 00:02:48,869
(Butler Francisco)

36
00:02:48,935 --> 00:02:50,103
Are you her guardian?

37
00:02:51,104 --> 00:02:52,572
Yes, I am.

38
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:55,008
You have to register at the counter.

39
00:02:55,375 --> 00:02:56,810
What is your name, ma'am?

40
00:02:57,544 --> 00:02:58,612
Park Bong Gon.

41
00:03:15,262 --> 00:03:16,363
Who are you?

42
00:03:34,981 --> 00:03:36,216
You already know, right?

43
00:03:39,453 --> 00:03:40,454
Yes.

44
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:58,338
She'll feel better now.

45
00:04:05,378 --> 00:04:06,413
Na Young.

46
00:04:07,714 --> 00:04:08,749
Class president.

47
00:04:08,949 --> 00:04:10,016
Are you awake now?

48
00:04:13,687 --> 00:04:14,855
How many fingers?

49
00:04:15,355 --> 00:04:16,356
One?

50
00:04:18,225 --> 00:04:19,760
This is Ms. Park Bong Gon.

51
00:04:19,826 --> 00:04:21,094
I'm Francesca.

52
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:26,700
Let's go somewhere else to talk.

53
00:04:27,567 --> 00:04:28,668
Can you get up?

54
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:43,950
Come in.

55
00:04:44,651 --> 00:04:47,354
No, you wait outside.

56
00:04:48,188 --> 00:04:49,923
I need to talk to her alone.

57
00:05:13,213 --> 00:05:14,214
Have a seat.

58
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,022
I heard about your family.

59
00:05:22,689 --> 00:05:25,592
I felt sorry for you,
so I rented out my place to you.

60
00:05:26,459 --> 00:05:28,895
Is your name also Francesca?

61
00:05:29,229 --> 00:05:30,530
That's correct.

62
00:05:30,597 --> 00:05:31,698
Just like yours.

63
00:05:32,866 --> 00:05:34,034
Anyway...

64
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:35,468
Have you drunk...

65
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,872
human blood for the first time recently?

66
00:05:39,873 --> 00:05:40,874
I have.

67
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:43,443
How did you know?

68
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:46,847
You kids are far too young
to be drinking fresh blood.

69
00:05:47,681 --> 00:05:49,516
It's only natural
you'd get blood sickness.

70
00:05:54,721 --> 00:05:57,257
Was it that boy's blood?

71
00:06:04,164 --> 00:06:05,165
What?

72
00:06:09,536 --> 00:06:10,537
No.

73
00:06:12,973 --> 00:06:14,140
That's good.

74
00:06:14,975 --> 00:06:16,309
It could've been disastrous.

75
00:06:17,110 --> 00:06:19,479
The stimulus must have been intense.

76
00:06:20,113 --> 00:06:24,551
The stronger the attachment,
the stronger the urge to drink blood.

77
00:06:26,152 --> 00:06:27,153
Attachment?

78
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:31,324
You really have no idea, do you?

79
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,237
Francesca.

80
00:06:45,705 --> 00:06:47,607
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

81
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:50,377
It's extremely important.

82
00:06:57,117 --> 00:06:58,418
What's going on?

83
00:06:58,485 --> 00:06:59,686
What's she telling her?

84
00:07:08,361 --> 00:07:10,163
They die?

85
00:07:11,331 --> 00:07:12,599
To be precise,

86
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:16,770
biting a human will still turn them
into a vampire, just like it used to.

87
00:07:17,170 --> 00:07:19,806
But the virus spreads immediately.

88
00:07:20,407 --> 00:07:22,108
They'll die within a year at most.

89
00:07:26,513 --> 00:07:27,647
Then...

90
00:07:27,714 --> 00:07:31,484
So if you really care about that boy,

91
00:07:32,485 --> 00:07:33,820
you should stay away from him.

92
00:07:36,523 --> 00:07:38,224
You'll spend the rest of your life
missing him...

93
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,593
and regretting it.

94
00:07:44,197 --> 00:07:45,398
I know. I've been there.

95
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:02,582
Today, you saved my life.

96
00:08:03,016 --> 00:08:04,851
If you're grateful, come visit sometime.

97
00:08:06,052 --> 00:08:08,555
I hardly have anyone
to play Go-Stop with...

98
00:08:09,389 --> 00:08:10,557
these days.

99
00:08:11,191 --> 00:08:12,359
What's Go-Stop?

100
00:08:12,625 --> 00:08:15,328
It's fun. I'll teach you.

101
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:18,264
Okay.

102
00:08:22,736 --> 00:08:23,737
Francesca.

103
00:08:29,042 --> 00:08:32,946
I sincerely hope you don't make
the same mistakes I did.

104
00:08:35,982 --> 00:08:36,983
Okay.

105
00:08:46,459 --> 00:08:47,594
Have a good night.

106
00:09:03,643 --> 00:09:06,513
We sure went through a lot today.

107
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:09,049
Yeah.

108
00:09:15,855 --> 00:09:17,524
Are you really okay?

109
00:09:19,125 --> 00:09:20,126
Yeah.

110
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,535
But...

111
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:32,439
shouldn't we talk about
what happened earlier?

112
00:09:35,108 --> 00:09:36,109
What?

113
00:09:37,844 --> 00:09:40,914
What we did earlier...

114
00:09:43,383 --> 00:09:44,384
The kiss...

115
00:09:48,555 --> 00:09:49,689
- Class president.
- Yeah?

116
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:53,159
Thanks for today. I should get going.

117
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,195
I'll walk with you. I live nearby too.

118
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:57,097
No, see you at school.

119
00:10:16,116 --> 00:10:17,250
Did you give her that blood?

120
00:10:22,355 --> 00:10:25,158
Isn't it only natural for vampires
to drink human blood?

121
00:10:26,259 --> 00:10:28,328
That doesn't change anything.

122
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:30,964
- Your parents...
- Then what about you?

123
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:34,300
You loved without regrets, so...

124
00:10:36,269 --> 00:10:37,470
Look how miserable you are now.

125
00:10:38,104 --> 00:10:39,139
I know.

126
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,795
Good morning.

127
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:37,964
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

128
00:11:38,031 --> 00:11:40,300
Are you all still asleep?

129
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:42,869
- Did you study?
- I did.

130
00:11:42,936 --> 00:11:44,070
Oh, really?

131
00:11:44,137 --> 00:11:45,605
- That's a lie.
- It's not.

132
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:48,741
Where did she go?

133
00:12:05,592 --> 00:12:07,160
Where are you? Are you skipping school?

134
00:12:09,596 --> 00:12:10,597
Aren't you hungry?

135
00:12:10,663 --> 00:12:12,599
- Let's go get dinner.
- I'm not hungry.

136
00:12:13,766 --> 00:12:15,969
Class president.
Were you looking for Pi Na Young?

137
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:17,604
She just came to school.

138
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:18,671
What?

139
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:23,776
Pi Na Young.

140
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:36,222
Dang it, my stomach hurts
when I run right after eating.

141
00:12:37,724 --> 00:12:39,192
How did he know I was here?

142
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:40,260
Pi Na Young.

143
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:41,828
You scared me.

144
00:12:43,363 --> 00:12:44,764
It's new seeing you get startled.

145
00:12:45,698 --> 00:12:47,634
What are you doing?
Why aren't you in class?

146
00:12:51,404 --> 00:12:53,606
I've had enough.

147
00:12:54,807 --> 00:12:55,808
What?

148
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,548
I don't enjoy studying.
Why would I work so hard for it?

149
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:04,851
All just to get free Wi-Fi.

150
00:13:04,917 --> 00:13:05,952
And school too.

151
00:13:06,019 --> 00:13:09,622
I only came here to eat.
I didn't come to play student.

152
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:13,493
- What are you talking...
- I don't need you anymore.

153
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:21,501
How stupid do you think I am?

154
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:24,971
At least put some effort into lying.

155
00:13:25,838 --> 00:13:27,340
Did you think I'd be hurt just enough...

156
00:13:27,407 --> 00:13:30,376
to accept that lousy excuse and back off?

157
00:13:31,077 --> 00:13:33,413
I don't know what that woman told you,

158
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:35,515
but I'm not going to just walk away...

159
00:13:36,215 --> 00:13:38,518
because you say you don't need me.

160
00:13:39,786 --> 00:13:40,920
And besides,

161
00:13:41,421 --> 00:13:42,555
I need to get into med scho...

162
00:13:42,622 --> 00:13:43,656
You might die!

163
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:50,830
If a vampire bites a human,
they get sick and die within a year.

164
00:13:51,130 --> 00:13:53,466
You won't get into med school
if you're dead.

165
00:13:53,533 --> 00:13:54,534
Got it?

166
00:13:56,369 --> 00:13:57,437
Now move.

167
00:13:58,104 --> 00:13:59,472
Then why did you kiss me?

168
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,680
What were we that day?

169
00:14:08,948 --> 00:14:09,949
What did it mean?

170
00:14:16,222 --> 00:14:18,224
Does that even matter now?

171
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:32,638
(Dooil High School)

172
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,248
I guess I can't eat here anymore.

173
00:14:43,783 --> 00:14:44,784
I'm hungry, though.

174
00:14:46,986 --> 00:14:47,987
Pi Na Young.

175
00:15:09,275 --> 00:15:11,210
You're more useful than I thought.

176
00:15:11,711 --> 00:15:14,080
Fine. I'll accept you as a friend.

177
00:15:15,281 --> 00:15:16,282
What about school?

178
00:15:20,286 --> 00:15:22,922
I'm done with school.

179
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,691
Really? Why?

180
00:15:29,529 --> 00:15:30,930
Because of Jang U Ju?

181
00:15:38,237 --> 00:15:39,906
Just think of him as a lunchbox.

182
00:15:40,706 --> 00:15:43,543
No one will even know
he died because you bit him.

183
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:47,613
Oh, no.

184
00:15:48,815 --> 00:15:49,849
Did I upset you?

185
00:15:52,819 --> 00:15:55,488
Do you like me?

186
00:15:56,889 --> 00:15:57,890
What?

187
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:58,958
Or...

188
00:15:59,592 --> 00:16:00,827
do you like U Ju?

189
00:16:00,893 --> 00:16:02,161
What are you talking about?

190
00:16:02,595 --> 00:16:03,663
Just...

191
00:16:04,030 --> 00:16:07,800
you seem awfully bothered
by me and him hanging out.

192
00:16:08,468 --> 00:16:09,702
Thanks for the food,

193
00:16:12,171 --> 00:16:13,473
but that's enough.

194
00:16:15,374 --> 00:16:16,375
Hey.

195
00:16:18,945 --> 00:16:22,181
Do you know what happens
when a human and a vampire get together?

196
00:16:25,785 --> 00:16:26,786
What happens?

197
00:16:29,555 --> 00:16:30,823
You get someone like me.

198
00:16:31,724 --> 00:16:34,594
My father was a vampire,
and my mother was human.

199
00:16:36,095 --> 00:16:40,633
It's pathetic how my dad
always missed my mom...

200
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:43,169
whom I've never even met.

201
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:47,840
I'm just worried you'll make
the same mistake.

202
00:16:49,108 --> 00:16:50,276
That's why I'm stepping in.

203
00:16:51,744 --> 00:16:54,614
So if you can't even control
that simple urge...

204
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:55,715
A simple urge?

205
00:16:57,850 --> 00:16:58,918
Desire?

206
00:17:03,155 --> 00:17:05,358
I've always gotten everything I've wanted.

207
00:17:05,925 --> 00:17:08,594
I've never hesitated
before eating something I wanted,

208
00:17:09,161 --> 00:17:11,230
or buying clothes I wanted to wear.

209
00:17:12,899 --> 00:17:13,900
So I'm saying...

210
00:17:14,834 --> 00:17:20,306
I'm not stupid enough
to mistake this for some simple urge.

211
00:17:21,774 --> 00:17:23,910
I don't know what you've been through,

212
00:17:24,510 --> 00:17:27,713
but whatever I'm feeling right now...

213
00:17:28,648 --> 00:17:29,815
I get to decide what it means.

214
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:31,817
Not you.

215
00:17:39,292 --> 00:17:41,994
(1st period: Korean Literature
2nd period: Math)

216
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:03,749
Oh, come on.

217
00:18:03,816 --> 00:18:05,952
(Report Card)

218
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,691
Why did your grades drop so much?

219
00:18:15,361 --> 00:18:16,362
Is it...

220
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:19,966
because of what I asked you before?

221
00:18:21,334 --> 00:18:24,170
You've done well up to now,

222
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:28,441
so you could still aim
for regular admission...

223
00:18:28,507 --> 00:18:31,944
He's been telling me in so many words
that I wouldn't get into med school.

224
00:18:32,011 --> 00:18:33,012
You're not dropping out, are you?

225
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:35,948
But it didn't bother me at all.
That was strange.

226
00:18:36,015 --> 00:18:37,316
I've seen students like that.

227
00:18:37,383 --> 00:18:40,219
It was almost as if I'd been put
under some spell.

228
00:18:41,387 --> 00:18:42,388
So...

229
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:45,124
Does that even matter now?

230
00:18:45,591 --> 00:18:46,692
I guess not.

231
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:49,161
Why did I say that?

232
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:50,963
What?

233
00:18:53,766 --> 00:18:54,967
Nothing.

234
00:18:55,334 --> 00:18:57,470
I understand. I'll get going.

235
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:08,881
(Pi Na Young)

236
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:19,191
(Pi Na Young)

237
00:19:22,261 --> 00:19:23,295
(CSAT Math)

238
00:19:30,603 --> 00:19:34,373
(U Ju told me to choose option 3
if I was stuck.)

239
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:39,578
(Why would Cheol Su do that?)

240
00:19:58,297 --> 00:19:59,832
Excuse me.

241
00:19:59,899 --> 00:20:00,900
Hey, young lady.

242
00:20:00,966 --> 00:20:02,168
You in the black dress!

243
00:20:06,405 --> 00:20:08,307
I'm a little weak.

244
00:20:08,841 --> 00:20:14,113
Could you push my wheelchair
to my house over there?

245
00:20:18,851 --> 00:20:19,852
Sure, no problem.

246
00:20:20,119 --> 00:20:21,487
Why, thank you.

247
00:20:30,262 --> 00:20:31,664
Oh, great.

248
00:20:31,731 --> 00:20:33,466
Let's go!

249
00:20:43,809 --> 00:20:44,877
Na Young?

250
00:20:46,645 --> 00:20:50,116
This should be far enough.

251
00:20:51,817 --> 00:20:55,087
Okay. Don't wander too far on your own.

252
00:20:58,958 --> 00:21:01,627
You're such a kind girl. Now I feel bad.

253
00:21:03,796 --> 00:21:05,197
Why would you feel bad?

254
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:06,632
You should be grateful.

255
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:12,872
No, I really do feel bad.

256
00:21:25,885 --> 00:21:26,919
Na Young?

257
00:21:32,491 --> 00:21:33,492
Na Young!

258
00:21:47,273 --> 00:21:48,908
The license plate...

259
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:51,544
It's 73 Heo 5067.

260
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:57,917
Hello, police?

261
00:21:58,918 --> 00:22:00,653
A person got kidnapped.

262
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:01,954
The license plate is...

263
00:22:02,788 --> 00:22:04,690
It's 73 Heo 5067.

264
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:07,459
Sorry? The location?

265
00:22:09,195 --> 00:22:10,196
Where am I?

266
00:22:17,136 --> 00:22:19,371
We'll look it up right away,

267
00:22:19,438 --> 00:22:21,841
but it might be impossible
to track it down.

268
00:22:21,907 --> 00:22:23,442
Let's wait for a bit.

269
00:22:31,417 --> 00:22:33,018
Okay, calm down. Think this through.

270
00:22:33,786 --> 00:22:34,787
What can I do?

271
00:22:35,521 --> 00:22:36,522
What now?

272
00:22:36,922 --> 00:22:38,390
My butler does everything for me.

273
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:39,859
Your butler?

274
00:22:39,925 --> 00:22:41,026
So you have one at home?

275
00:22:41,493 --> 00:22:42,494
Not now.

276
00:22:42,561 --> 00:22:43,562
He's out for work.

277
00:22:44,563 --> 00:22:45,998
Her butler...

278
00:22:50,469 --> 00:22:52,571
What? She got kidnapped?

279
00:22:52,638 --> 00:22:54,273
Yes, what should I do?

280
00:22:55,007 --> 00:22:56,008
Why would she...

281
00:22:57,343 --> 00:22:58,344
Is there a way?

282
00:23:01,313 --> 00:23:02,314
There is.

283
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:03,782
What is it?

284
00:23:03,849 --> 00:23:06,385
I set up location sharing on her phone...

285
00:23:06,619 --> 00:23:08,487
because she's always all over the place.

286
00:23:08,988 --> 00:23:10,556
I'll send the link to you now.

287
00:23:10,756 --> 00:23:11,757
Okay, thanks.

288
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,095
Ms. Francesca...

289
00:23:18,597 --> 00:23:20,933
Sir, make a U-turn.

290
00:23:21,166 --> 00:23:22,268
Here?

291
00:23:22,568 --> 00:23:24,169
If I do that here,

292
00:23:24,236 --> 00:23:27,039
we'll both be on the news
tomorrow morning.

293
00:23:27,106 --> 00:23:28,173
Oh, but...

294
00:23:31,677 --> 00:23:33,846
Ms. Francesca!

295
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:35,414
(Truck Helper)

296
00:23:36,482 --> 00:23:37,650
(Checking Location)

297
00:23:37,716 --> 00:23:38,751
(Current Location)

298
00:23:39,018 --> 00:23:40,019
I found her.

299
00:23:40,886 --> 00:23:41,921
Hey, taxi.

300
00:23:42,187 --> 00:23:44,356
Taxi!

301
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:49,361
Oh, what do I do?

302
00:23:49,428 --> 00:23:51,463
Okay, calm down. Try to think.

303
00:23:55,067 --> 00:23:56,101
Need a lift?

304
00:23:57,670 --> 00:23:58,704
You...

305
00:23:58,771 --> 00:23:59,805
Hop on.

306
00:24:03,509 --> 00:24:05,144
What? Will you walk instead?

307
00:24:29,568 --> 00:24:30,569
What is this?

308
00:24:34,106 --> 00:24:35,641
We've been waiting...

309
00:24:36,809 --> 00:24:38,711
a long time for your kind.

310
00:24:40,612 --> 00:24:41,647
For what?

311
00:24:41,714 --> 00:24:42,715
Your kind is...

312
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:50,556
You're a vampire.

313
00:24:52,458 --> 00:24:55,194
I don't know what you're talking about.

314
00:24:55,394 --> 00:24:57,730
You don't need to pretend.

315
00:24:57,796 --> 00:25:00,733
We all know about it.

316
00:25:12,678 --> 00:25:14,847
So what do you want from me?

317
00:25:18,117 --> 00:25:19,118
So...

318
00:25:20,152 --> 00:25:22,354
Just bite us.

319
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:25,357
What?

320
00:25:25,424 --> 00:25:27,359
You have immortality and eternal life...

321
00:25:28,127 --> 00:25:31,096
all to yourselves. That's not fair!

322
00:25:32,564 --> 00:25:35,834
You could share it with us, couldn't you?

323
00:25:36,668 --> 00:25:37,903
What the heck is this?

324
00:25:40,172 --> 00:25:43,976
We want to become vampires like you.

325
00:25:44,043 --> 00:25:45,677
It's easy.

326
00:25:45,744 --> 00:25:47,880
Just bite us here and draw some blood...

327
00:25:47,946 --> 00:25:49,448
Wait, will it leave a scar?

328
00:25:49,515 --> 00:25:50,516
Maybe.

329
00:25:50,582 --> 00:25:52,017
Really? Then bite somewhere else...

330
00:25:52,918 --> 00:25:54,820
Just give us one bite right here...

331
00:25:54,887 --> 00:25:58,624
and draw some blood.

332
00:25:58,690 --> 00:25:59,958
That's how we...

333
00:26:00,025 --> 00:26:01,093
No.

334
00:26:01,693 --> 00:26:02,694
I can't do that.

335
00:26:03,962 --> 00:26:05,464
Damn it.

336
00:26:05,998 --> 00:26:09,835
I didn't expect you to agree so easily.

337
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:11,804
Well, it can't be helped.

338
00:26:12,037 --> 00:26:15,941
Big guy, go get the equipment.

339
00:26:17,142 --> 00:26:19,845
- Yes, sir.
- Damn it.

340
00:26:38,530 --> 00:26:39,798
Hallelujah!

341
00:26:42,568 --> 00:26:44,870
- Praise the Lord!
- Oh, Father!

342
00:26:44,937 --> 00:26:47,339
Bless us with your grace!

343
00:26:47,906 --> 00:26:49,541
Father Almighty...

344
00:26:50,409 --> 00:26:51,610
Damn it.

345
00:26:55,948 --> 00:26:57,316
Are you done yet?

346
00:26:59,017 --> 00:27:00,419
Can you untie me already?

347
00:27:01,053 --> 00:27:05,457
Hey, none of this is working.

348
00:27:12,731 --> 00:27:13,899
Are you sure she's a vampire?

349
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:18,036
- Is she?
- What?

350
00:27:18,103 --> 00:27:20,239
I told you to find the right one!

351
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:22,040
I saw the footage!

352
00:27:22,107 --> 00:27:24,243
She came back to life, just like...

353
00:27:49,535 --> 00:27:50,536
Here.

354
00:27:51,203 --> 00:27:52,804
You like this, don't you?

355
00:27:54,072 --> 00:27:56,542
Come on. Bite me!

356
00:28:13,825 --> 00:28:15,127
The signal stopped here.

357
00:28:18,730 --> 00:28:19,932
That means...

358
00:28:32,744 --> 00:28:33,745
Hey.

359
00:28:35,914 --> 00:28:37,349
Why are you suddenly helping me?

360
00:28:38,517 --> 00:28:41,286
Is it some kind of vampire solidarity?

361
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:42,888
I don't know.

362
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:44,723
Watching you two together,

363
00:28:44,790 --> 00:28:47,659
I guess I wanted to be the bridge
for two star-crossed lovers.

364
00:28:48,026 --> 00:28:49,127
Cut the crap.

365
00:28:49,928 --> 00:28:50,929
It just...

366
00:28:52,364 --> 00:28:54,366
reminds me of my dad.

367
00:28:55,234 --> 00:28:56,335
I got curious...

368
00:28:56,902 --> 00:28:58,704
about what it's like
to love someone for a year...

369
00:28:58,770 --> 00:29:00,672
and miss them for the rest of your life.

370
00:29:11,583 --> 00:29:15,087
I told you, you idiots.

371
00:29:15,153 --> 00:29:17,155
If I bite you, you'll die.

372
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,925
Don't you get it? You'll die!

373
00:29:22,461 --> 00:29:26,732
Do you really think
we'd believe that nonsense?

374
00:29:27,266 --> 00:29:28,267
Bite me!

375
00:29:40,579 --> 00:29:42,147
You people!

376
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:49,054
What's going on here?

377
00:29:50,389 --> 00:29:51,490
Who are you?

378
00:29:51,556 --> 00:29:52,557
Class president!

379
00:29:52,924 --> 00:29:53,925
Hey.

380
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:58,530
Oh, you're one of her kind too.

381
00:29:58,897 --> 00:30:01,400
Well, that makes things easier.

382
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:04,169
Then maybe you could...

383
00:30:04,236 --> 00:30:06,071
We have no intention of biting you.

384
00:30:07,939 --> 00:30:10,008
And we don't want any trouble.

385
00:30:11,143 --> 00:30:13,211
Just put away those useless props.

386
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:15,013
We can talk this out peacefully...

387
00:30:16,248 --> 00:30:17,249
Hey, you...

388
00:30:17,316 --> 00:30:19,418
Are you okay?

389
00:30:25,057 --> 00:30:26,391
I was hoping we could
settle this peacefully,

390
00:30:28,293 --> 00:30:29,428
but I guess that's not happening.

391
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:48,413
Oh, it hurts!

392
00:30:55,354 --> 00:30:57,422
Stop kicking me!

393
00:31:04,730 --> 00:31:05,731
What are you doing?

394
00:31:06,365 --> 00:31:07,432
Are you just going to lie there?

395
00:31:32,858 --> 00:31:33,859
Gosh.

396
00:31:42,501 --> 00:31:45,103
You look too healthy
to be pushed in a wheelchair.

397
00:31:48,273 --> 00:31:49,908
Just bite me once.

398
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:52,511
No.

399
00:31:53,111 --> 00:31:54,179
Please.

400
00:31:54,479 --> 00:31:55,480
No.

401
00:31:57,149 --> 00:31:58,216
Bite me.

402
00:31:58,283 --> 00:31:59,317
No.

403
00:31:59,384 --> 00:32:00,519
- Do it!
- No!

404
00:32:00,819 --> 00:32:03,588
Just bite me once. Please, just...

405
00:32:03,655 --> 00:32:04,689
I said no.

406
00:32:33,318 --> 00:32:34,619
I knew.

407
00:32:34,853 --> 00:32:36,121
U Ju!

408
00:32:37,289 --> 00:32:40,625
I knew Pi Na Young would come back
even if she fell.

409
00:32:42,561 --> 00:32:43,829
I knew that, but...

410
00:33:12,624 --> 00:33:13,625
Jang U Ju!

411
00:33:17,329 --> 00:33:18,330
U Ju...

412
00:33:19,464 --> 00:33:20,665
No...

413
00:33:25,337 --> 00:33:26,538
It's my...

414
00:33:26,972 --> 00:33:28,106
first time...

415
00:33:29,307 --> 00:33:30,342
seeing you cry.

416
00:33:31,610 --> 00:33:32,844
Why is that important now?

417
00:33:34,479 --> 00:33:35,480
What do we do?

418
00:33:37,215 --> 00:33:38,216
Do something.

419
00:33:41,786 --> 00:33:43,054
There's only one way.

420
00:33:53,565 --> 00:33:54,566
No.

421
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:56,801
He'll die within a year.

422
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:58,603
He'll die anyway
if we leave him like this.

423
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:06,211
It's your choice,

424
00:34:07,178 --> 00:34:08,179
Francesca.

425
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:27,899
Jang U Ju.

426
00:34:30,535 --> 00:34:31,536
Pi Na Young?

427
00:34:37,576 --> 00:34:38,577
Now,

428
00:34:39,311 --> 00:34:42,514
I've got good news and bad news for you.

429
00:34:44,249 --> 00:34:45,417
Which do you want to hear first?

430
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:49,421
The bad news.

431
00:34:50,188 --> 00:34:51,456
The bad news is,

432
00:34:52,490 --> 00:34:55,160
you've got one year left to live, at most.

433
00:34:59,831 --> 00:35:01,132
And the good news is...

434
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,835
The great-aunt is here.

435
00:35:31,630 --> 00:35:32,697
Welcome...

436
00:35:35,266 --> 00:35:36,301
to the world of vampires.

437
00:35:41,006 --> 00:35:44,075
The son of blood!

438
00:35:44,576 --> 00:35:47,245
- The son of blood!
- The son of blood!

439
00:36:07,666 --> 00:36:10,602
(Francesca Next Door)

440
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:14,626
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
